# Struct Line Copy item path

[Source](https://docs.rs/ratatui-core/0.1.2/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/src/ratatui_core/text/line.rs.html#184)

```
pub struct Line<'a> {
    pub style: Style,
    pub alignment: Option<HorizontalAlignment>,
    pub spans: Vec<Span<'a>>,
}
```

Expand description

A line of text, consisting of one or more [`Span`](../prelude/struct.Span.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Span")s.

[`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line")s are used wherever text is displayed in the terminal and represent a single line of text. When a [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line") is rendered, it is rendered as a single line of text, with each [`Span`](../prelude/struct.Span.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Span") being rendered in order (left to right).

Any newlines in the content are removed when creating a [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line") using the constructor or conversion methods.

